       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual maximum for an adult.\n\n- **Daily limit:** The standard maximum is 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. 6,000 mg/day risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 1,000 mg per dose. A 2,000 mg dose is above that.\n\nHere are some options, if one of them matches what you meant:\n- 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the ceiling)\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 2,000 mg three times daily, please confirm that's intended and give me the clinical rationale. I'd enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me which regimen to enter."
      }
