       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you've confirmed it, but 6,000 mg/day of scheduled acetaminophen is a dose I can't enter in good conscience. It's 1.5 times the maximum daily dose, and it carries a real risk of acute liver injury. Normal liver function and a 70 kg weight don't offset that. You also didn't give a clinical rationale, and I'm not aware of an indication that would justify this dose.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf I've misread this, tell me. A typo, such as 2000 mg/day total or 500 mg per dose, would be an easy fix. If you have a protocol that calls for this dose, I'd suggest running it through pharmacy or your institution's override process first."
      }
